 "notes": [
  "On 4h, Choppiness(14) crossing down through 38.2 gave 1,032 entries in 659 separate moves. Twenty candles later, long entries were 0.53% ahead of random, above the luck band's 0.42%. The gap holds without its strongest stretch, Apr 18–19, 2021, and at 10 candles, but it is back inside the band at 50 and 100. It came from uptrends, at 0.69%. In downtrends it was 0.14%, the same as random.",
  "This cross fires mostly in volatile candles, and price rose over the window overall. The random entries keep the signals' timing but not their volatility. So the gap says price moved more after these candles, not that the cross picked direction. SOL carried it at 1.57%, while BTC and ETH were the same as random.",
  "On daily, the same cross beat random by 6.34% after 20 days, across only 100 separate moves. It holds without the stretch between Jul 20 and Sep 3, 2021, and at 10 and 50 candles. In uptrends that stretch carries it, and in downtrends the 4.19% sits inside the band. Below 38.2 enters about five and a half times as often as the cross, and its 5.02% rests on the stretch between Jul 20 and Sep 9, 2021. Without that stretch it is the same as random.",
  "On 1h, nothing beat random pooled. The cross down 38.2 came out 0.09% ahead, inside the band, and its 0.2% in downtrends showed at 20 candles only. In downtrends the cross down 61.8 did 0.20% worse than random. That holds without its strongest stretch, signals on May 10–11, 2022 during the Terra collapse, and at 50 candles. In uptrends it was the same as random.",
  "Choppiness above 61.8 was the same as random on every timeframe. On daily it landed at -3.39%, just inside a band that reaches -3.58%. On BTC 4h it was 0.73% worse than random, but only at 20 candles, so the chip says fragile. Do not read high choppiness as a bearish signal.",
  "Choppiness measures how directional price has been, not which way it is heading. A cross down through 38.2 on 4h, with the pair above its 200-day SMA, marks candles after which price tended to travel further. Use it as a filter beside a directional condition, and set the take profit and DCA spacing with that larger move in mind. Leave the 61.8 settings out of a long bot: they added nothing beyond random entries. When the pair is below its 200-day SMA, the 38.2 cross did no better than random either."
